// MOVED from the passing corpus (temporal_only/0524): this policy's forbid
// guard sums `a`, whose ONLY occurrence is in the LEFT operand of a `since`.
// Range restriction propagates only through the since-RIGHT (the anchor), so
// the formula is non-monitorable: `since`-left is a CONTINUITY condition
// ("Transfer::response(a) held at every step since the login"), not a
// collection. At any request decision point that relation is empty — the sum
// is 0 on every trace, so the guard was dead code — and when a Login request
// is itself the decision point the anchor range (j, i] is empty, the left is
// vacuously true for EVERY `a`, and the relation is infinite (the evaluator
// fabricated 0). The case's own trace shows the authored intent was "sum of
// resolved transfer amounts since login" (three 501s, total 1503, against a
// 1500 threshold — built to trip the forbid), which the formula as written
// cannot express; the recorded `true` at the Read merely documented the inert
// guard. The validator now rejects the formula: an aggregation `for`-variable
// must be range-restricted by a positive atom of the `where` body.
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (total: Long). ((sum a for (a: Long). where (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::response{ input.user: context.input.user, input.amount: a } since within 2h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user })) == total && total > 1500)};
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
